<title>UK: French poised to jump on London United bus - paper.</title>
<headline>French poised to jump on London United bus - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A state-owned French company is poised to take control of one of London's last big independent bus companies -- London United -- for around 50 million pounds, the Financial Times said.</p>
<p>The newspaper reported that Transdev, a subsidiary of Caisse des Depots et Consignations, was close to finalising terms in what would be the first foray of a continental player into the UK bus market.</p>
<p>London United operates on 40 routes in south-west and central London and holds around nine percent of the London market.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
